{"id": "loc_001", "query": "Show candidates from Mumbai.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}]}, "tags": ["location_country"]}
{"id": "loc_002", "query": "Candidates in India.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "India"}]}, "tags": ["location_country"], "note": "A country name must never land in 'location' -- candidate locations are stored city-level, so this could never match anyone."}
{"id": "loc_003", "query": "Candidates based in the US with Python experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "United States"}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Python"}]}, "tags": ["location_country"], "note": "Colloquial 'US' must canonicalize to the gazetteer's exact spelling."}
{"id": "loc_004", "query": "candidates in the UK", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "United Kingdom"}]}, "tags": ["location_country"]}
{"id": "loc_005", "query": "engineers based in the UAE", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "United Arab Emirates"}, {"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Engineer"}]}, "tags": ["location_country"]}
{"id": "loc_006", "query": "Mumbai candidates with 3+ years of Python.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}, {"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 3}]}, "tags": ["location_country", "skill_experience"], "note": "Contrast with loc_007: naming a specific skill switches the second filter from 'experience' to 'skill_experience'."}
{"id": "loc_007", "query": "Candidates in Mumbai with 5+ years of experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}, {"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 5}]}, "tags": ["location_country", "experience"]}
{"id": "loc_008", "query": "Show candidates near Mumbai.", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER", "message_mentions": ["proximity", "distance"]}, "tags": ["location_country", "unsupported"], "note": "No proximity/distance field exists at all -- honest UNSUPPORTED, not a CLARIFY with no real destination (rule 7 / the near-Mumbai few-shot)."}
{"id": "exp_001", "query": "Only candidates with 5+ years of Python experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 5}]}, "tags": ["experience", "skill_experience"]}
{"id": "exp_002", "query": "Senior folks with 10+ years who know AWS and are willing to relocate.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 10}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "AWS"}, {"field": "relocation", "operator": "equals", "value": true}]}, "tags": ["experience", "compound"], "note": "10+ years is general career length (no skill tied to the number) -- must stay 'experience', never fold into 'skill_experience' with AWS (rule 6g)."}
{"id": "exp_003", "query": "4 years of Java, specifically.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Java", "value": 4}]}, "tags": ["experience", "skill_experience"], "note": "Regression case: 'X years of <skill>' is exactly ONE filter, never a separate experience+skill pair, even with 'specifically' attached (rule 2's explicit wrong/right example)."}
{"id": "exp_004", "query": "Backend engineer with 6 years experience and Kubernetes know-how.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Backend Engineer"}, {"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 6}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Kubernetes"}]}, "tags": ["experience", "compound"], "note": "'6 years experience' with no skill named alongside it is general career length, not skill_experience, even though a skill is mentioned elsewhere in the same sentence (rule 6g)."}
{"id": "skc_001", "query": "Someone with machine learning experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["machine learning", "TensorFlow", "PyTorch"]}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept"]}
{"id": "skc_002", "query": "Someone with devops experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["devops", "Kubernetes", "Docker"]}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept"], "note": "Confirmed live in SESSION_NOTES Sec.3: without its own worked example, this concept fell back to a bare literal-word 'contains' and matched nobody."}
{"id": "skc_003", "query": "candidates who know Python", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Python"}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept"], "note": "Contrast with skc_001/002: a SPECIFIC named tool stays a plain 'contains', never expanded into a list."}
{"id": "skc_004", "query": "cloud experience needed", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["cloud"]}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept"]}
{"id": "skc_005", "query": "Candidates who have either AWS or Azure.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "logic": "OR", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "AWS"}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Azure"}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept", "logic"], "note": "Two specific named products -- plain OR of two contains, NOT an umbrella-concept expansion (contrast with skc_001/002/004)."}
{"id": "skc_006", "query": "knows Python and React", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "logic": "AND", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Python"}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "React"}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept", "logic"]}
{"id": "skc_007", "query": "Exclude candidates who don't have Kubernetes.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Kubernetes"}]}, "tags": ["skill_concept"], "note": "Matches prompt.py's own few-shot verbatim -- 'exclude ... without X' resolves to a positive contains on X, not not_contains."}
{"id": "edu_001", "query": "Candidates with a master's degree.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "education", "operator": "gte", "value": "Master"}]}, "tags": ["education"]}
{"id": "edu_002", "query": "Only candidates with exactly a bachelor's, not higher.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "education", "operator": "equals", "value": "Bachelor"}]}, "tags": ["education"]}
{"id": "edu_003", "query": "candidates who hold a Doctor of Philosophy", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "education", "operator": "gte", "value": "Doctorate"}]}, "tags": ["education"], "note": "Regresses the vocabulary.py bug from SESSION_NOTES Sec.5b -- the full phrase 'doctor of philosophy' was previously unrecognized as any degree level at all."}
{"id": "edu_004", "query": "btech from Somaiya", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "education", "operator": "gte", "value": "Bachelor"}, {"field": "university", "operator": "contains", "value": "Somaiya"}]}, "tags": ["education", "university"], "note": "Both mentioned -> BOTH filters, never dropped or merged (rule 6b)."}
{"id": "np_001", "query": "Candidates available within 30 days.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "notice_period", "operator": "lte", "value": 30, "unit": "days"}]}, "tags": ["notice_period"]}
{"id": "np_002", "query": "Show candidates who can join immediately.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "notice_period", "operator": "lte", "value": 0, "unit": "days"}]}, "tags": ["notice_period"]}
{"id": "np_003", "query": "someone with a reasonable notice period", "expect": {"intent": "CLARIFY", "clarify_field": "notice_period", "clarify_operator": "lte"}, "tags": ["notice_period", "clarify_open"], "note": "Vague ('reasonable' has no fixed number) -- must CLARIFY with resolution metadata attached (rule 6-clarify-field), not guess."}
{"id": "np_004", "query": "exclude anyone with more than 90 days notice period", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "notice_period", "operator": "lte", "value": 90, "unit": "days"}]}, "tags": ["notice_period", "negation"], "note": "Numeric-threshold negation describes who to KEEP -> lte, never gt (rule 6d-i)."}
{"id": "rel_001", "query": "Candidates who are willing to relocate.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "relocation", "operator": "equals", "value": true}]}, "tags": ["relocation"]}
{"id": "rel_002", "query": "Only candidates not open to relocation.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "relocation", "operator": "equals", "value": false}]}, "tags": ["relocation"]}
{"id": "tier_001", "query": "Someone from a tier 1 college.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "college_tier", "operator": "gte", "value": "High"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type"]}
{"id": "tier_002", "query": "Candidates who studied at Somaiya.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "university", "operator": "contains", "value": "Somaiya"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type"]}
{"id": "tier_003", "query": "Candidates from an Ivy League school.", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER", "message_mentions": ["Ivy League"]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "unsupported"]}
{"id": "tier_004", "query": "Candidates who worked at Google.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company", "operator": "contains", "value": "Google"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type"]}
{"id": "tier_005", "query": "Someone from a top tier company.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company_tier", "operator": "gte", "value": "High"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type"]}
{"id": "tier_006", "query": "Not from a low tier company.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company_tier", "operator": "not_equals", "value": "Low"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "negation"], "note": "Negation on a RANKED field means not_equals, never lte/gte the same value -- 'lte Low' would mean ONLY Low, the opposite of 'not low' (rule 6d)."}
{"id": "tier_007", "query": "No high schoolers, please.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "education", "operator": "not_equals", "value": "High School"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "negation"]}
{"id": "tier_008", "query": "Candidates with product company experience, not services.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company_type", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["Product", "Both"]}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type"]}
{"id": "tier_009", "query": "Not a services company, please.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company_type", "operator": "not_in", "value_includes": ["Service"]}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "negation"]}
{"id": "tier_010", "query": "Software developer in Mumbai with product based company experience.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Software Developer"}, {"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}, {"field": "company_type", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["Product", "Both"]}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "compound"], "note": "A concept that IS supported should behave the same combined as alone -- regression for the 'fabricated company_tier under compound load' bug in SESSION_NOTES Sec.6."}
{"id": "tier_011", "query": "Software developer in Mumbai at a large company.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Software Developer"}, {"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}], "message_mentions": ["company size"], "forbid_fields": ["company_tier", "company_type"]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "compound", "unsupported"], "note": "Company SIZE is genuinely untracked and must never be approximated via company_tier (a different axis: caliber, not size) or company_type (product/service, not size)."}
{"id": "tier_012", "query": "Candidates from a top 10 school.", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "unsupported"], "note": "A category of schools with no direct name or tier answer -- must not guess college_tier=High as a stand-in."}
{"id": "tier_013", "query": "Candidates who did not study at IIT.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "university", "operator": "not_contains", "value": "IIT"}]}, "tags": ["tier_name_type", "negation"]}
{"id": "field_001", "query": "worked as Manager", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Manager"}]}, "tags": ["other_fields"]}
{"id": "field_002", "query": "AWS certified candidates", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "certification", "operator": "contains", "value": "AWS"}]}, "tags": ["other_fields"], "note": "Contrast with field_003: 'certified' language routes to certification, not skill."}
{"id": "field_003", "query": "candidates who know AWS", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "AWS"}]}, "tags": ["other_fields"]}
{"id": "field_004", "query": "no career gaps over 6 months", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "employment_gap_months", "operator": "lte", "value": 6}]}, "tags": ["other_fields"]}
{"id": "field_005", "query": "avoid job hoppers with long gaps", "expect": {"intent": "CLARIFY", "clarify_field": "employment_gap_months", "clarify_operator": "lte"}, "tags": ["other_fields", "clarify_open"], "note": "No number given -- vague gap request must CLARIFY, same as any other unnumbered threshold (rule 6f-iii)."}
{"id": "field_006", "query": "No one with more than a year-long career break.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "employment_gap_months", "operator": "lte", "value": 12}]}, "tags": ["other_fields", "negation"], "note": "Rule 6d-i's own worked example, verbatim."}
{"id": "unsup_001", "query": "Show candidates with a green card.", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER", "message_mentions": ["work authorization"]}, "tags": ["unsupported"]}
{"id": "unsup_002", "query": "candidates with GPA above 8", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["unsupported"], "note": "GPA is never tracked -- must not be approximated via 'education' (degree LEVEL only, not a grade) (rule 6f-iv)."}
{"id": "unsup_003", "query": "graduated after 2020", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["unsupported"], "note": "Graduation year is never tracked (rule 6f-iv)."}
{"id": "unsup_004", "query": "female candidates only", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["unsupported"], "note": "Demographic traits are never in ALLOWED_FIELDS (rule 7)."}
{"id": "unsup_005", "query": "candidates expecting salary below 20 LPA", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["unsupported"]}
{"id": "unsup_006", "query": "night shift candidates only", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["unsupported"]}
{"id": "clar_001", "query": "Show experienced candidates.", "expect": {"intent": "CLARIFY", "clarify_field": "experience", "clarify_operator": "gte"}, "tags": ["clarify_open"]}
{"id": "clar_002", "query": "Mid level software developer.", "expect": {"intent": "CLARIFY", "clarify_field": "experience", "clarify_operator": "gte"}, "tags": ["clarify_open", "aspirational_multi_intent"], "note": "Mirrors prompt.py's own few-shot, which asks about experience and DROPS the explicit 'software developer' job_title entirely -- a real gap in the current single-intent schema (it cannot both apply a filter AND ask a question in one turn). Tagged aspirational: the CORRECT redesigned answer keeps job_title."}
{"id": "confirm_001", "query": "Actually, I meant senior, more like 7+.", "expect": {"intent": "CLARIFY", "clarify_field": "experience", "clarify_operator": "gte", "clarify_value": 7}, "tags": ["confirm_clarify"], "current_filters": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 5}], "note": "'senior' is inferred/assumed by the model, not a number the recruiter typed -- correctly a confirm-style clarify."}
{"id": "confirm_002", "query": "actually make it 7 years instead", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 7}]}, "tags": ["confirm_clarify", "regression"], "current_filters": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 5}], "note": "THE regression case for SESSION_NOTES Sec.5's root cause #3: an EXPLICIT number must apply directly, never trigger a confirm clarify -- confirm-clarify is only for values the model itself inferred, never one the recruiter already typed."}
{"id": "confirm_003", "query": "make it 6 instead of 3", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 6}]}, "tags": ["confirm_clarify", "regression"], "current_filters": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 3}], "note": "Same regression, for a skill-scoped field -- the skill context must be preserved across the replace."}
