{"id": "lookup_004", "query": "what's his email address", "expect": {"intent": "UNSUPPORTED_FILTER"}, "tags": ["lookup", "unsupported"], "note": "A question about one candidate, but email maps to no ALLOWED_FIELDS concept at all -- UNSUPPORTED, not a fabricated LOOKUP."}
{"id": "merge_001", "query": "Actually, show Bangalore instead.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Bangalore"}]}, "tags": ["merge"], "current_filters": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Mumbai"}], "note": "Must REPLACE the existing location filter, not add a second, conflicting one."}
{"id": "merge_002", "query": "actually make it 5 years", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 5}]}, "tags": ["merge"], "current_filters": [{"field": "skill_experience", "operator": "gte", "skill": "Python", "value": 3}], "note": "Skill context ('Python') must survive the replace even though the reply only restates the number."}
{"id": "merge_003", "query": "actually the US instead", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "United States"}]}, "tags": ["merge"], "current_filters": [{"field": "country", "operator": "equals", "value": "India"}]}
{"id": "filler_001", "query": "candidates from good universities", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "college_tier", "operator": "gte", "value": "High"}]}, "tags": ["filler_guard", "model_choice_sensitive"], "note": "'good' is a quality cue -> college_tier, never a literal university named 'good' (validation.py's GENERIC_FILLER_WORDS catches the literal-name case defensively, but the model should route correctly in the first place)."}
{"id": "filler_002", "query": "someone from a big company", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "company_tier", "operator": "gte", "value": "High"}]}, "tags": ["filler_guard", "model_choice_sensitive"]}
{"id": "comp_001", "query": "8+ years, knows Kubernetes, and open to relocating.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 8}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Kubernetes"}, {"field": "relocation", "operator": "equals", "value": true}]}, "tags": ["compound"]}
{"id": "comp_002", "query": "8+ years, Kubernetes, and open to relocating, at a large company.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "experience", "operator": "gte", "value": 8}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "Kubernetes"}, {"field": "relocation", "operator": "equals", "value": true}], "message_mentions": ["company size"], "forbid_fields": ["company_tier"]}, "tags": ["compound", "unsupported"], "note": "One genuinely unsupported clause mixed with three valid ones -- apply the real filters and say honestly what couldn't be applied, never fabricate a field for it and never drop the whole query to UNSUPPORTED_FILTER."}
{"id": "asp_001", "query": "Bangalore fintech folks, senior, payments experience, can start soon.", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "predicates": [{"field": "location", "operator": "equals", "value": "Bangalore"}, {"field": "skill", "operator": "contains", "value": "payments"}], "message_mentions": ["industry"]}, "tags": ["aspirational_multi_intent"], "note": "Ideal: apply location + skill, ask about seniority AND notice period as two separate queued questions, report industry as untracked -- all in one turn. Not representable today."}
{"id": "asp_002", "query": "backend engineers who know either Go or Rust, from a product company, not Infosys", "expect": {"intent": "FILTER_CANDIDATES", "logic": "AND", "predicates": [{"field": "job_title", "operator": "contains", "value": "Backend Engineer"}, {"field": "company_type", "operator": "in", "value_includes": ["Product", "Both"]}, {"field": "company", "operator": "not_contains", "value": "Infosys"}]}, "tags": ["aspirational_multi_intent", "logic"], "note": "AND-over-a-group-containing-OR ((Go OR Rust) AND product AND NOT Infosys) -- FilterSpec.logic is a single flat value across all filters today, so mixed boolean structure like this cannot be expressed at all, only approximated by dropping the OR."}
